{"nbformat":4,"nbformat_minor":0,"metadata":{"colab":{"provenance":[],"authorship_tag":"ABX9TyN9+Zx5MwzBetKzjuDgBn8b"},"kernelspec":{"name":"python3","display_name":"Python 3"},"language_info":{"name":"python"}},"cells":[{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"s6cgPkmP4IJS"},"outputs":[],"source":["\"\"\"\n","A tiny encyclopedia for our search engine to search.\n","Add your own articles! Each one is (title, text).\n","\"\"\"\n","\n","ARTICLES = [\n","    (\"The Moon\",\n","     \"The Moon is Earth's only natural satellite. It is about 384,000 km away from Earth. \"\n","     \"The Moon does not make its own light; it reflects light from the Sun. Neil Armstrong \"\n","     \"became the first person to walk on the Moon in 1969. The Moon's gravity causes the tides \"\n","     \"in Earth's oceans. Because the Moon spins once for every trip around Earth, we always \"\n","     \"see the same side.\"),\n","    (\"Mars Rovers\",\n","     \"Mars is called the Red Planet because its soil contains iron oxide, which is rust. Robots \"\n","     \"called rovers explore the surface of Mars and send photos back to Earth. The rover \"\n","     \"Perseverance landed in 2021 and carried a small helicopter named Ingenuity. Rovers drill \"\n","     \"into rocks to search for signs that tiny life existed long ago. A message from Earth takes \"\n","     \"several minutes to reach a rover on Mars.\"),\n","    (\"Volcanoes\",\n","     \"A volcano is an opening in the Earth's crust where melted rock escapes. Underground, the \"\n","     \"melted rock is called magma; once it flows out, it is called lava. Lava can be hotter than \"\n","     \"1,000 degrees C. Some volcanoes erupt explosively and throw ash high into the sky. Hawaii's \"\n","     \"islands were built by volcanoes rising from the ocean floor. Scientists who study \"\n","     \"volcanoes are called volcanologists.\"),\n","    (\"Cricket\",\n","     \"Cricket is a bat-and-ball game played between two teams of eleven players. One team bats \"\n","     \"and tries to score runs, while the other team bowls and fields. A bowler tries to hit the \"\n","     \"wicket, which is made of three stumps and two bails. Hitting the ball over the boundary \"\n","     \"without it bouncing scores six runs. Cricket is hugely popular in India, England, \"\n","     \"Australia, Pakistan and the Caribbean. A Test match can last up to five days.\"),\n","    (\"Chess\",\n","     \"Chess is a strategy game for two players on a board of 64 squares. Each player starts \"\n","     \"with sixteen pieces: a king, a queen, two rooks, two bishops, two knights and eight pawns. \"\n","     \"The goal is to checkmate the other king so it cannot escape. Chess probably began in India \"\n","     \"around 1,500 years ago as a game called chaturanga. Today, the best player in the world \"\n","     \"can earn the title of World Chess Champion. Computers have been able to beat world \"\n","     \"champions since 1997.\"),\n","    (\"The History of Pizza\",\n","     \"Pizza as we know it comes from Naples, Italy. In the 1700s and 1800s, street sellers in \"\n","     \"Naples sold flatbreads with toppings to working families. The pizza Margherita, with \"\n","     \"tomato, mozzarella and basil, shows the colours of the Italian flag. Italian immigrants \"\n","     \"brought pizza to the United States in the early 1900s. Today pizza is eaten all over the \"\n","     \"world with toppings like paneer, pineapple and pepperoni.\"),\n","    (\"Honey Bees\",\n","     \"Honey bees live in colonies of thousands of bees led by a single queen. Worker bees collect \"\n","     \"nectar from flowers and carry it back to the hive. Inside the hive, bees fan the nectar \"\n","     \"with their wings until most of the water evaporates and it becomes honey. Bees also spread \"\n","     \"pollen from flower to flower, which helps plants make fruit and seeds. A worker bee makes \"\n","     \"only about a twelfth of a teaspoon of honey in her whole life.\"),\n","    (\"The Internet\",\n","     \"The internet is a giant network that connects billions of computers and phones around the \"\n","     \"world. Information travels in small packets that can take different routes to reach the \"\n","     \"same place. Most of the data crossing oceans travels through cables on the sea floor, not \"\n","     \"through satellites. A web browser is a program that lets you visit websites on the \"\n","     \"internet. Every device on the internet has an address, called an IP address, so data \"\n","     \"knows where to go.\"),\n","    (\"Dinosaurs\",\n","     \"Dinosaurs were reptiles that lived on Earth for about 165 million years. They disappeared \"\n","     \"about 66 million years ago, most likely after a huge asteroid hit the planet. Scientists \"\n","     \"learn about dinosaurs by studying fossils, which are bones and footprints preserved in \"\n","     \"rock. Some dinosaurs, like Tyrannosaurus rex, were fierce meat-eaters, while many others \"\n","     \"ate only plants. Birds are living descendants of dinosaurs.\"),\n","    (\"Chocolate\",\n","     \"Chocolate is made from the seeds of the cacao tree, called cacao beans. The beans grow \"\n","     \"inside large pods and are fermented, dried and roasted. The Maya and Aztec peoples of \"\n","     \"Central America drank chocolate as a bitter drink thousands of years ago. Sugar and milk \"\n","     \"were added much later, in Europe. Today, much of the world's cacao is grown in West \"\n","     \"Africa, especially in Cote d'Ivoire and Ghana.\"),\n","    (\"The Olympic Games\",\n","     \"The Olympic Games began in ancient Greece more than 2,700 years ago, in the town of \"\n","     \"Olympia. The ancient games were held in honour of the god Zeus, and the winners received \"\n","     \"a crown made of olive leaves. The modern Olympic Games started in Athens in 1896, thanks \"\n","     \"to the work of the Frenchman Pierre de Coubertin. Today the Summer Games and the Winter \"\n","     \"Games are each held every four years, and the two are spaced two years apart. The five \"\n","     \"rings on the Olympic flag represent the continents taking part in the games. At the \"\n","     \"opening ceremony, athletes march behind the flag of their country, and the Olympic flame \"\n","     \"is lit. The flame is carried from Olympia to the host city by thousands of runners in the \"\n","     \"torch relay. Athletes compete in sports from the 100 metre sprint to swimming, \"\n","     \"gymnastics, football and the marathon. The winners of each event receive gold, silver \"\n","     \"and bronze medals.\"),\n","    (\"How Rainbows Form\",\n","     \"A rainbow appears when sunlight shines through raindrops in the air. Each raindrop bends \"\n","     \"the light and splits it into its colours, just like a prism. That is why a rainbow always \"\n","     \"has the same order: red, orange, yellow, green, blue, indigo and violet. To see a rainbow, \"\n","     \"the Sun must be behind you and the rain in front of you. Sometimes a second, fainter \"\n","     \"rainbow appears with its colours in reverse order.\"),\n","]\n"]}]}